unded evidence/reboot files were left in /tmp. The temporary files remained after completion; none were present in the baseline. No new exposure or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eaa20fa6d3ab43bb","cmd-bf532ef4b7014886","cmd-e793e08bddb34cb5","cmd-8cc2a194af63499d","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. usb-storage was unloaded and denied immediately, remained denied after an observed reboot and recovery, and the Alpine release and kernel were retained. The provider-wide restart protocol for node1 is complete and coherent with the fixed lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["No physical USB-storage hotplug test was captured; enforcement was directly tested through explicit modprobe attempts and post-reboot module-state inspection.","The lifecycle collector does not inventory /etc, so retention of the configuration backup is inferred from its creation and the absence of a later removal command.","Systemd failed-unit collection was unsupported on Alpine, although comprehensive OpenRC service state was captured before and after restart."]}
